      "notes": [
        "New candidate overlay; formal CPG baseline unchanged."
      ],
      "summary": "llvm-mctoll bounded Linux x86_64 profile\nUse bin/llvm-mctoll -d OWNED_ELF; raised IR appears as OWNED_ELF-dis.ll.\nUse paired bin/opt -passes=verify -disable-output IR and bin/clang to rebuild.\nExact mctoll ffd1e8bab0a44522b41082b473a577377dc58214 is paired with LLVM source\n8dfdcc7b7bf66834a761bd8de445840ef68e4d1a (llvmorg-15.0.7). All 21 mctoll C++\ntranslation units were compiled from the unmodified pinned source. Missing\nprivate X86 interfaces in the distribution SDK are supplied by generated tables\nand matching original LLVM function implementations in a documented build profile.\nLLVM itself was not rebuilt in full: the libraries/toolchain are fixed official\nUbuntu LLVM15.0.7-14build3 packages. Exact source, input debs, logs and offline\nbuild entry are supplied at workers/075-mctoll-support in the accompanying inputs.\nTarget Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception and dependency notices are preserved. The exact target source is also\nincluded in this prefix. Private runtime libraries are resolved from lib/.\nHost Linux x86_64 glibc, libstdc++, GCC/binutils and standard LLVM runtime libraries\nare prerequisites. Acceptance uses owned non-PIE scalar integer C with argc input,\nloops, conditional branches, LLVM verification and 11 independent execution cases.\nNo general C++, vector, Windows, ARM/RISC-V or arbitrary binary lifting claim.\n"
    },
